#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:1
msgid "ADR-0005: Propagation methods and planner rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-16"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P4.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:9
msgid ""
"LUMOS propagates fields from any grid to any grid (REQ-PROP-1/2) and must"
" choose the numerical method automatically, log the choice and allow "
"forcing it (REQ-PROP-4). Each method is accurate only in a domain set by "
"the sampling of the field, the distance and the output grid; a wrong "
"choice gives aliased or approximate fields without any error message. The"
" plan asked for \"transfer function, impulse response, two steps\" "
"Fresnel methods and for scaled or shifted angular spectra (MFT or CZT)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:15
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:17
msgid ""
"**Methods.** Six kernels, all pure functions of backend arrays "
"(ADR-0002), applied to every polarisation component, mode and wavelength:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "Output grid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "Domain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "`rs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "any"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "everywhere (direct sum, cost `N_in N_out`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "`fraunhofer`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "far field, focal plane of a lens, Fraunhofer regime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "`fresnel_tf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "input grid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "Fresnel regime, `dx ≳ λz/L`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "`fresnel_ir`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "Fresnel regime, `dx ≲ λz/L`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "`fresnel_mft`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "Fresnel regime, chirp sampled over the field support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "`asm`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md
msgid "spectrum inside the Matsushima band limit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:29
msgid ""
"The \"two-step\" Fresnel method of the plan is replaced by `fresnel_mft`,"
" a one-step Fresnel transform evaluated with a matrix Fourier transform: "
"it gives any output sampling and centre directly, which is what the two-"
"step scheme was meant to provide. Scaled and shifted angular spectra use "
"an inverse matrix Fourier transform rather than a chirp-z transform: same"
" result, simpler code, and the cost is dominated by the FFT for the grid "
"sizes of interest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:35
msgid ""
"**Planner.** The planner measures the spatial support and the spectral "
"support of the actual field (boxes holding `1 - 1e-6` of the power) and "
"applies, for every wavelength, these rules in order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:38
msgid "`distance=None` → `fraunhofer`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:39
msgid "`z < 0` → `asm` (exactly invertible);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:40
msgid ""
"spectral support inside the band limit and output inside the padded "
"window → `asm`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:41
msgid ""
"neglected Fresnel phase `k ρ⁴ / 8z³ ≤ 0.01` rad → `fresnel_mft` if the "
"chirped field is sampled and the output frequencies avoid the periodic "
"replicas, otherwise `fresnel_ir` / `fresnel_tf` on the input grid (split "
"at the critical distance `N dx² / λ`);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:44
msgid "input quadratic phase `k ρ_in² / 2z ≤ 0.05` rad → `fraunhofer`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:45
msgid "otherwise `rs`, with a warning above `1e10` operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:47
msgid ""
"A wavecube or bundle uses one method for all its channels: the most "
"conservative per-wavelength choice. The decision and its reason are "
"logged on `lumos.propagation` and available without propagating through "
"`lumos.propagation.plan()`. An explicit `method=` bypasses the planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:51
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:53
msgid ""
"Choosing from the grids only (sampling criteria such as `z_c = N dx² / "
"λ`): simpler, but blind to the actual bandwidth of the field; a smooth "
"beam is propagated exactly by the angular spectrum far beyond `z_c`, "
"while a sharp aperture is not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:56
msgid ""
"Always using the angular spectrum with large padding: exact but memory-"
"hungry at long distances, and it cannot reach the far field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:58
msgid ""
"Chirp-z transforms for scaled outputs: equivalent results, more code; can"
" be added later as a kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:60
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:62
msgid ""
"Every rule is checked by the validation suite (P4.1) and by Hypothesis "
"batteries against analytic solutions (P4.6), which demonstrate a valid "
"choice in all tested cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:64
msgid ""
"Supports are computed with an FFT of up to 16 representative fields on "
"the host: the planner runs outside compiled code. Compiled pipelines "
"should fix the method once (from `plan()`) and call the kernel directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0005-propagation-planner.md:66
msgid ""
"New methods register with `lumos.propagation.register_method`; the "
"planner must be extended explicitly."
msgstr ""
